# Computational Thinking for Problem Solving — C Programming Lab Workbook

A cumulative question bank of **97 C programming questions** from Experiments 2–10 (First Year, Semester I, AY 2026-27), with an empty code block under each question for your solution.

> Experiment 1 (algorithms and flowcharts) is not included. Questions that repeated across experiments or answer sheets appear only once.

## Contents

| Exp | Topic | Questions |
|---|---|---|
| 2 | [Variables, Data Types, Operators, Expressions and I/O in C](#experiment-2--variables-data-types-operators-expressions-and-io-in-c) | 11 |
| 3 | [Conditional Branching (if-else, switch-case)](#experiment-3--conditional-branching-if-else-switch-case) | 17 |
| 4 | [Looping Control Structures (for, while, do-while)](#experiment-4--looping-control-structures-for-while-do-while) | 23 |
| 5 | [Nested Loops and Loop Control (break, continue)](#experiment-5--nested-loops-and-loop-control-break-continue) | 7 |
| 6 | [One-Dimensional Arrays](#experiment-6--one-dimensional-arrays) | 9 |
| 7 | [Two-Dimensional Arrays and Strings](#experiment-7--two-dimensional-arrays-and-strings) | 8 |
| 8 | [Functions, Recursion, Inline Functions and Macros](#experiment-8--functions-recursion-inline-functions-and-macros) | 10 |
| 9 | [Structures and Pointers](#experiment-9--structures-and-pointers) | 8 |
| 10 | [File Handling (Files and Streams)](#experiment-10--file-handling-files-and-streams) | 4 |
| | **Total** | **97** |

## How to use

1. Find the question you want to solve.
2. Paste your program into the empty `c` code block under **Answer:**.
3. Change `- [ ] Solved` to `- [x] Solved` when you're done.

Works the same on GitHub and in [Obsidian](https://obsidian.md): headings are unique (`Exp4 · Q7`), so you can jump to them from the outline panel or link to them.

## Suggested repo layout

```text
.
├── README.md        # this workbook
└── solutions/       # optional: full .c files, one per question
    ├── exp2_q1.c
    └── ...
```

---

